#: ../../source/config_product.rst:3
msgid "Assemblies and scenes"
msgstr "装配体与场景"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:9
msgid "Assemblies"
msgstr "装配体"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:12
msgid "Declare assemblies"
msgstr "声明装配体"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:14
msgid ""
"Assemblies are defined using the ``partcad.yaml`` file in the package "
"folder. The syntax for defining assemblies is as follows:"
msgstr "装配体使用包目录中的 ``partcad.yaml`` 文件来定义。定义装配体的语法如下："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:60
msgid ""
"The ``assy`` type is used to define assemblies in `Assembly YAML` format,"
" and the ``step`` type reads the structure out of a STEP file (see "
":ref:`assembly_step`). The ``urdf`` type reads a robot description as an "
"assembly directly (see :doc:`simulation`). A format an engine's plugin "
"package implements is named through that package -- ``sim-mujoco:mjcf`` "
"for a MuJoCo model, which is also a :ref:`scene <scenes>` type, the "
"section that declares it being what decides which it is. The ``path`` "
"parameter specifies the source file path, and the ``parameters`` section "
"allows for defining parameters that can be used within the assembly. The "
"source file does not have to be a part of the package: ``fileFrom`` and "
"``fileUrl`` pull it from a remote location on first use, exactly as they "
"do for :ref:`parts` (see :ref:`files`). This holds for every assembly "
"type -- a vendor's STEP assembly is declared with its URL and read from "
"there."
msgstr ""
"``assy`` 类型用于以 `Assembly YAML` 格式定义装配体，而 ``step`` 类型则从 STEP 文件中读取其结构（参见 "
":ref:`assembly_step` ）。 ``urdf`` 类型直接把机器人描述当作装配体读取（参见 :doc:`simulation` "
"）。由某个引擎的插件包实现的格式，要通过该包来指名——例如 MuJoCo 模型的 ``sim-mujoco:mjcf`` ，它同时也是一种 "
":ref:`场景 <scenes>` 类型，究竟算哪一种，取决于声明它的小节。 ``path`` 参数指定源文件路径，而 "
"``parameters`` 小节用于定义可在装配体内部使用的参数。源文件不必是包的一部分： ``fileFrom`` 和 ``fileUrl``"
" 会在首次使用时从远程位置拉取它，方式与 :ref:`parts` 完全相同（参见 :ref:`files` "
"）。这对每一种装配体类型都成立——供应商的 STEP 装配体可以用它的 URL 来声明，并从那里读取。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:73
msgid ""
"``timeout`` is for an assembly that is known to be slow. PartCAD waits "
"five minutes for the daemon to say *something* while it works, and one "
"large assembly built or rendered in a sandbox can say nothing for longer "
"than that; one that declares ``timeout: 1800`` is waited on for half an "
"hour instead, for as long as it is being worked on. It never shortens the"
" wait, and it does not change the assembly's cache key. Declaring it also"
" marks the assembly as slow: ``--fast-only`` leaves it out of a render, a"
" test or a listing, which is what a sweep over a large tree in CI wants "
"(see :ref:`fast-only`). A scene takes the same key."
msgstr ""
"``timeout`` 用于那些已知很慢的装配体。PartCAD 在守护进程工作期间最多等待五分钟以听到 *某种* "
"动静，而一个在沙箱中构建或渲染的大型装配体可能在更长的时间里毫无声息；声明了 ``timeout: 1800`` "
"的装配体则会被等待半小时，只要它仍在被处理。它绝不会缩短等待时间，也不会改变装配体的缓存键。声明它同时还会把该装配体标记为慢： ``--fast-"
"only`` 会把它排除在渲染、测试或列表之外，而这正是在 CI 中扫描一棵大型树时所需要的（参见 :ref:`fast-only` "
"）。场景使用同样的键。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:83
msgid ""
"``dependencies`` is for the files the source file pulls in by itself -- a"
" Jinja macro file, another ``.assy`` it includes. The parts and "
"assemblies an ``assy`` file links to need no listing there: an assembly's"
" cache key covers theirs, so editing one of them rebuilds every assembly "
"using it. The same holds for the sketch of an ``extrude`` or ``sweep`` "
"part, and for the assembly a ``compound`` part is made from."
msgstr ""
"``dependencies`` 用于源文件自行引入的那些文件——一个 Jinja 宏文件，或它所包含的另一个 ``.assy`` 文件。 "
"``assy`` "
"文件所链接到的零件和装配体无需列在那里：装配体的缓存键已经涵盖了它们的缓存键，所以编辑其中任何一个，都会让使用它的每一个装配体重新构建。对于 "
"``extrude`` 或 ``sweep`` 零件所用的草图，以及 ``compound`` 零件所基于的装配体，情况也一样。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:93
msgid "Ports and interfaces of an assembly"
msgstr "装配体的端口与接口"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:95
msgid ""
"An assembly is connected to other things the way a part is: by its ports,"
" and by the interfaces those ports belong to (see :ref:`interfaces`). "
"What it does not have is a part's way of getting them. A part is one "
"solid and says where its ports are on it; an assembly is made of parts "
"that already carry ports, already placed -- and an assembly's port is one"
" of those, seen from outside."
msgstr ""
"装配体与其他东西相连的方式和零件一样：通过它的端口，以及这些端口所属的接口（参见 :ref:`interfaces` "
"）。它所没有的，是零件获得这些端口的那套办法。零件是单个实体，它直接说明端口位于自身的什么位置；而装配体是由已经携带端口、并且已经被放置好的零件组成的——装配体的端口就是其中之一，只不过是从外部来看的。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:101
msgid ""
"So an assembly does not state a coordinate somebody worked out by hand. "
"It says which one it means:"
msgstr "因此装配体不会给出某人手工算出的坐标。它只说明自己指的是哪一个："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:116
msgid ""
"The key is the new name. The value names what is being externalized: two "
"elements are **a node and one of its ports**, three are **a node, an "
"interface it implements and the instance of it**. Nothing else changes as"
" a result: a mapped port is a port of this assembly like any other, and a"
" mapped interface instance brings in exactly what an ``implements:`` of "
"the same interface would have -- the same port names (``mount-3mm-thru-"
"opening-m3``), the same freedom of movement, and the same ancestors, so "
"an assembly that externalizes an ``m4-thru-3`` can be connected as an "
"``m4-thru`` like anything else."
msgstr ""
"键是新的名称。值则指明被对外暴露的是什么：两个元素表示 **一个节点和它的一个端口** ，三个元素表示 "
"**一个节点、它所实现的一个接口，以及该接口的实例** "
"。除此之外没有任何变化：被映射的端口就是这个装配体的普通端口，而被映射的接口实例所带来的内容，与对同一接口写 ``implements:`` "
"完全一致——相同的端口名称（ ``mount-3mm-thru-opening-m3`` ）、相同的运动自由度、相同的祖先接口，因此一个对外暴露 "
"``m4-thru-3`` 的装配体，可以像其他任何东西一样作为 ``m4-thru`` 来连接。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:125
msgid ""
"What the map does **not** do is rename an interface. The interface is "
"read off the node and kept: it is a contract, and an assembly is in no "
"position to restate one. The *instance* name is the assembly's to choose,"
" because an instance is a place rather than a kind -- the bracket calls "
"it ``outer``, and the mount it is part of calls it ``mount``."
msgstr ""
"映射 **不会** 做的事情是重命名接口。接口是从节点上读取出来并原样保留的：它是一份契约，而装配体没有资格重新表述它。至于 *实例* "
"的名称，则由装配体自行选择，因为实例代表的是位置而不是种类——支架把它叫做 ``outer`` ，而包含该支架的安装件把它叫做 ``mount``"
" 。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:132
msgid "Which nodes can be named"
msgstr "哪些节点可以被指名"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:134
msgid ""
"The first element is the **node name from the Assembly YAML file** -- a "
"link's ``name:``, or the part or assembly name where the link has none "
"(see :doc:`assy`) -- and not the name of the part. An assembly places the"
" same part six times; five of those are not the one being externalized."
msgstr ""
"第一个元素是 **Assembly YAML 文件中的节点名称** ——即某个 link 的 ``name:`` ，或者在 link "
"没有名称时所用的零件名或装配体名（参见 :doc:`assy` "
"）——而不是零件的名称。一个装配体可能把同一个零件放置六次；其中五次都不是要被对外暴露的那一个。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:139
msgid ""
"The anonymous ``links:`` containers an ASSY file is built out of "
"contribute nothing to the name: they are the file's own structure rather "
"than things, so every node is named exactly as the file names it however "
"deeply the file nests it. A node inside a *named* container is reached "
"through it, with ``/``::"
msgstr ""
"构成 ASSY 文件的那些匿名 ``links:`` "
"容器对名称没有任何贡献：它们属于文件自身的结构，而不是实际的东西，因此无论文件把节点嵌套得多深，每个节点的名称都与文件中给它的名称完全一致。位于 "
"*有名称的* 容器内部的节点，则要用 ``/`` 经由该容器来访问::"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:147
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A node name may be written in terms of the assembly's own parameters, the"
" way ``ports:`` and ``implements:`` may be -- ``map: {mount: "
"[\"%which%\", handle]}`` -- which is how an assembly parametrized by what"
" it holds externalizes the right one."
msgstr ""
"节点名称可以用装配体自身的参数来书写，就像 ``ports:`` 和 ``implements:`` 那样—— ``map: {mount: "
"[\"%which%\", handle]}`` ——以自己所持有的东西为参数的装配体，正是这样对外暴露出正确的那一个。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:152
msgid ""
"A sub-assembly that some package declares is a different matter: it is an"
" object with a boundary of its own, and the map does not reach inside it."
" To reach a port in there, that sub-assembly externalizes it and this one"
" maps *that*. A boundary is crossed one object at a time, which is what "
"keeps an assembly free to be rearranged inside without breaking whatever "
"connects to it."
msgstr ""
"由某个包声明的子装配体则是另一回事：它是拥有自身边界的对象，映射无法伸进它的内部。要访问其中的端口，需由那个子装配体先把端口对外暴露，然后本装配体再映射"
" *那个* 端口。边界一次只跨越一层，正是这一点让装配体可以自由地重新调整内部结构，而不会破坏与它相连的任何东西。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:159
msgid "What a map cannot say"
msgstr "映射无法表达的东西"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:161
msgid ""
"Some of an assembly's connections are not a port of anything inside it --"
" the face a fixture is clamped by, a datum the whole product is aligned "
"to. Those are declared the way a part declares them, with ``ports:`` and "
"``implements:``, which an assembly takes in exactly the same spelling as "
":ref:`parts`."
msgstr ""
"装配体的某些连接并不是它内部任何东西的端口——比如夹具夹持的那个面，或整个产品对齐所依据的基准。这些要像零件那样，用 ``ports:`` 和 "
"``implements:`` 来声明；装配体接受的写法与 :ref:`parts` 完全相同。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:166
msgid ""
"The two are read in order: the map first, then ``ports:``, then "
"``implements:``. So a declaration may refer to what the map produced -- "
"an ``implements:`` instance may sit at a mapped port instead of at a "
"coordinate:"
msgstr ""
"它们是按顺序读取的：先是映射，然后是 ``ports:`` ，最后是 ``implements:`` 。因此声明可以引用映射所产生的结果—— "
"``implements:`` 的实例可以位于某个被映射的端口上，而不必位于某个坐标上："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:181
msgid ""
"A ``ports:`` entry that uses a name the map already produced wins, and "
"says so in the log: two things under one name is a mistake worth hearing "
"about."
msgstr "如果 ``ports:`` 条目使用了映射已经产生的名称，则以该条目为准，并且会在日志中说明这一点：同一个名称下有两样东西，是一个值得被提醒的错误。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:185
msgid "The boundary"
msgstr "边界"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:187
msgid ""
"What an assembly externalizes is what it *has*, everywhere: ``pc info`` "
"lists those ports, the viewer marks them, ``pc render --with-ports`` "
"draws them, a ``connect:`` in an ASSY file reaches them, and ``pc search "
"--interface`` finds the assembly by them. What is inside it and not "
"externalized is its own business. An assembly that declares no ``map:``, "
"no ``ports:`` and no ``implements:`` therefore has no ports at all -- "
"which is the answer to \"what can I connect to this\", not a failure. "
"``pc render --with-internals`` looks inside one anyway, for finding the "
"connection that went wrong (see :doc:`cli`)."
msgstr ""
"装配体对外暴露的东西，就是它在任何场合所 *拥有* 的东西： ``pc info`` 会列出这些端口，查看器会把它们标出来， ``pc "
"render --with-ports`` 会把它们画出来，ASSY 文件中的 ``connect:`` 可以访问它们，而 ``pc search"
" --interface`` 可以通过它们找到该装配体。至于它内部那些没有被对外暴露的东西，则是它自己的事。因此，一个既没有声明 ``map:``"
" ，也没有声明 ``ports:`` 和 ``implements:`` "
"的装配体根本没有任何端口——这是对“我能把什么连到它上面”这个问题的回答，而不是一种失败。 ``pc render --with-"
"internals`` 仍然可以查看它的内部，用来找出出错的连接（参见 :doc:`cli` ）。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:197
msgid "Other assembly types"
msgstr "其他装配体类型"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:199
msgid ""
"``map:`` is written for ``assy``, where the node names are the ones "
"somebody wrote in the file. It works for ``step`` and ``urdf`` assemblies"
" as best it can -- the nodes are then the components or the links, named "
"as the imported file names them, which is not something this package "
"controls. Where that does not fit, those assemblies state their ports the"
" way a part does, with ``ports:`` and ``implements:``."
msgstr ""
"``map:`` 是为 ``assy`` 设计的，那里的节点名称是有人写在文件里的。对于 ``step`` 和 ``urdf`` "
"装配体，它会尽力工作——此时节点是组件或连杆，名称由被导入的文件决定，而这并不是本包所能控制的。在不适用的场合，这些装配体就像零件那样，用 "
"``ports:`` 和 ``implements:`` 来声明自己的端口。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:208
msgid ""
"**Manufacturing.** ``assy`` is the only manufacturing method an assembly "
"has: it is put together by following the instructions in its own Assembly"
" YAML file, rather than made the way a part is. Every assembly of type "
"``assy`` gets that method with the type, so ``manufacturing`` never has "
"to be spelled out:"
msgstr ""
"**制造。** ``assy`` 是装配体唯一的制造方式：它是按照自己的 Assembly YAML "
"文件中的说明装配起来的，而不是像零件那样被制造出来。每个 ``assy`` 类型的装配体都随类型一起获得该方式，因此 "
"``manufacturing`` 永远不必写明："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:221
msgid ""
"Whether an assembly is *held to* that -- whether ``pc test`` checks that "
"its parts can be obtained and its connection instructions followed -- is "
"what ``manufacturable`` says, exactly as for parts."
msgstr ""
"装配体是否要 *受此约束* ——即 ``pc test`` 是否会检查它的零件能否获得、它的连接说明能否被执行——由 "
"``manufacturable`` 来决定，这与零件完全一致。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:225
msgid ""
"The optional ``offset`` parameter specifies the location of the assembly "
"using an OCCT Location object. See \"Implementation Detail\" for more "
"information on the OCCT Location object."
msgstr ""
"可选的 ``offset`` 参数使用一个 OCCT Location 对象来指定装配体的位置。关于 OCCT Location "
"对象的更多信息，请参见“Implementation Detail”。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:228
msgid "Here is an example of an assembly definition:"
msgstr "下面是一个装配体定义的示例："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:242
msgid ""
"In this example, an assembly named ``example_assembly`` is defined with a"
" parameter ``length`` and an offset."
msgstr "在这个示例中，定义了一个名为 ``example_assembly`` 的装配体，它带有一个参数 ``length`` 和一个偏移量。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:245
msgid "URDF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:247
msgid ""
"The ``urdf`` type uses a `URDF <https://wiki.ros.org/urdf>`_ file - the "
"robot description format of ROS - as an assembly directly, with no "
"conversion step:"
msgstr ""
"``urdf`` 类型直接把 `URDF <https://wiki.ros.org/urdf>`_ 文件——ROS "
"的机器人描述格式——用作装配体，不需要任何转换步骤："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:261
msgid ""
"``pc add assembly urdf <path>`` writes that declaration for a URDF that "
"is already inside the package. ``pc import assembly <path>`` is the other"
" choice: it converts instead of declaring, leaving the package with an "
"``stl`` part per link, an interface pair per joint and an ``.assy``, "
"exactly as ``pc convert assembly -t assy`` does below. Both commands work"
" the way they do for a STEP file - ``add`` points at a file, ``import`` "
"turns one into PartCAD's own objects."
msgstr ""
"``pc add assembly urdf <path>`` 会为已经位于包内的 URDF 写出这段声明。另一个选择是 ``pc import "
"assembly <path>`` ：它进行转换而不是声明，会在包中留下每个连杆一个 ``stl`` 零件、每个关节一对接口，以及一个 "
"``.assy`` 文件，与下文的 ``pc convert assembly -t assy`` 完全一样。这两个命令的行为与处理 STEP "
"文件时相同—— ``add`` 指向一个文件，而 ``import`` 把文件变成 PartCAD 自己的对象。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:269
msgid ""
"**One part per shape, in one flat list.** A link that has a single "
"``<visual>`` (or ``<collision>``) becomes the part ``<assembly "
"name>/<link name>``. A link that has several becomes a *sub-assembly* of "
"one part each, named ``<assembly name>/<link name>/<element name or "
"index>``. Every link is a direct child of the assembly, placed where the "
"joints between it and the robot's root link put it with **every joint at "
"its zero position**, and each shape keeps the offset its own ``<origin>``"
" gave it. The result is the same in-memory representation an `Assembly "
"YAML`_ file produces, so everything else - rendering, export, BoM, "
"inspection - treats the two alike. The assembly is the container that "
"holds the links, the robot's root link included; it is not one of them "
"and carries no properties of its own."
msgstr ""
"**每个形状一个零件，排成一张扁平的列表。** 只有一个 ``<visual>`` （或 ``<collision>`` ）的连杆会变成零件 "
"``<assembly name>/<link name>`` 。有多个的连杆则会变成一个 *子装配体* ，其中每个形状一个零件，名为 "
"``<assembly name>/<link name>/<element name or index>`` "
"。每个连杆都是装配体的直接子节点，其位置由它与机器人根连杆之间的那些关节在 **每个关节都处于零位** 时所决定，而每个形状都保留它自己的 "
"``<origin>`` 给出的偏移。其结果与 `Assembly YAML`_ "
"文件所产生的内存表示完全相同，因此其余的一切——渲染、导出、物料清单、查看——对两者一视同仁。装配体是容纳这些连杆（包括机器人的根连杆）的容器；它本身不是其中之一，也不携带任何属于自己的属性。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:281
msgid ""
"The joint tree deliberately does not become nesting. A URDF's tree is its"
" *kinematics*, and an assembly is one static configuration of it, so a "
"link hanging off another says nothing that the link's own placement does "
"not already say - while nesting per joint would make an arm as deep as it"
" has joints. The relative placements are not lost: they are what ``pc "
"convert assembly -t assy`` turns into joints, below. The only nesting "
"left is the one that means something, a link whose several shapes group "
"together."
msgstr ""
"关节树刻意不会变成嵌套结构。URDF 的树描述的是它的 *运动学* "
"，而装配体是它的一个静态构型，所以一个挂在另一个之下的连杆，说不出该连杆自身的放置位置没有说出的任何东西——而按关节嵌套则会让一条机械臂的深度等于它的关节数。相对位置关系并没有丢失：它们正是下文"
" ``pc convert assembly -t assy`` "
"转化为关节的内容。唯一保留下来的嵌套是有意义的那一种：一个连杆的多个形状归在一起。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:289
msgid ""
"Those parts are ordinary parts. ``pc ide view robot/forearm`` and ``pc "
"export -t step robot/wrist`` work on them like on any other. They are not"
" declared in ``partcad.yaml`` - the URDF is what declares them - so a "
"package handed one of these names builds the assembly that owns it first."
msgstr ""
"这些零件就是普通的零件。 ``pc ide view robot/forearm`` 和 ``pc export -t step "
"robot/wrist`` 对它们的作用与对任何其他零件一样。它们并没有在 ``partcad.yaml`` 中声明——声明它们的是 "
"URDF——因此当包接到这样一个名称时，会先构建拥有它的那个装配体。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:294
msgid ""
"**Nothing is rewritten that does not have to be.** A ``mesh`` reference "
"becomes a part that reads the very file the URDF named (``package://``, "
"``file://`` and paths relative to the URDF file are all resolved), for "
"the mesh formats PartCAD reads - ``stl``, ``obj``, ``step``, ``brep`` and"
" ``3mf``. The ``<origin>`` that places it becomes a PartCAD location, not"
" a transform baked into a copy of the geometry. A mesh ``scale`` is "
"honoured: URDF reads mesh coordinates as metres after scaling, PartCAD "
"works in millimetres. Only ``box``, ``cylinder`` and ``sphere`` are "
"generated, because there is no file to point at."
msgstr ""
"**不必改写的东西一概不改写。** 对于 PartCAD 能读取的网格格式—— ``stl`` 、 ``obj`` 、 ``step`` 、 "
"``brep`` 和 ``3mf`` ——一个 ``mesh`` 引用会变成一个零件，该零件读取的正是 URDF 所指明的那个文件（ "
"``package://`` 、 ``file://`` 以及相对于 URDF 文件的路径都会被解析）。放置它的 ``<origin>`` "
"会变成一个 PartCAD 位置，而不是被烘焙进几何体副本里的变换。网格的 ``scale`` 会被遵守：URDF "
"在缩放之后按米来解读网格坐标，而 PartCAD 以毫米为单位工作。只有 ``box`` 、 ``cylinder`` 和 ``sphere`` "
"会被生成出来，因为没有文件可供指向。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:303
msgid ""
"A link that states both a visual and a collision shape is built from the "
"**collision** one: that is what a simulator resolves contact against, and"
" a model that bothers to state both means it to be the physical shape. "
"``ignoreCollision: true`` reverses that for every link, and a list of "
"link names reverses it for those links only."
msgstr ""
"同时给出了视觉形状和碰撞形状的连杆，会以 **碰撞** "
"形状来构建：仿真器正是用它来求解接触的，而一个特意同时给出两者的模型，意在让它成为物理形状。 ``ignoreCollision: true`` "
"会对每个连杆反转这一行为，而给出一个连杆名称列表，则只对这些连杆反转。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:309
msgid ""
"What a link says about its physics becomes **named PartCAD properties** "
"of the part, one property per URDF value and in PartCAD's own units: "
"``<inertial>`` becomes ``mass``, ``centerOfMass`` and ``inertia``, and "
"the friction and contact settings of a ``<gazebo>`` block become "
"``friction``, ``contactStiffness`` and the rest. Its ``<material>`` "
"becomes ``material`` and ``color``. Nothing is stashed under a container "
"of its own, nothing records the link's name or its parent - the part *is*"
" named after the link, and the joint tree is this very file - and URDF "
"that PartCAD has no property for stops the import rather than being "
"carried opaquely. ``strict`` extends that to ``<gazebo>``, whose "
"vocabulary is open and where an unknown setting is otherwise only "
"reported."
msgstr ""
"连杆关于自身物理属性的描述，会变成该零件的 **具名 PartCAD 属性** ，每个 URDF 值对应一个属性，并采用 PartCAD "
"自己的单位： ``<inertial>`` 会变成 ``mass`` 、 ``centerOfMass`` 和 ``inertia`` ，而 "
"``<gazebo>`` 块中的摩擦与接触设置会变成 ``friction`` 、 ``contactStiffness`` 等等。它的 "
"``<material>`` 会变成 ``material`` 和 ``color`` "
"。没有任何东西被塞进专属于自己的容器里，也没有任何东西记录连杆的名称或它的父节点——零件本身 *就是* "
"以连杆命名的，而关节树就是这个文件本身——至于 PartCAD 没有对应属性的那些 URDF 内容，会直接中止导入，而不是被不透明地带过去。 "
"``strict`` 把这一做法扩展到 ``<gazebo>`` ：它的词汇表是开放的，其中未知的设置在默认情况下只会被报告出来。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:320
msgid ""
"The geometry a link was *not* built from is kept too, as the part "
"``<assembly name>/<link name>/<visual|collision>``: defined and "
"exportable, but not placed in the assembly. What cannot be represented at"
" all (joint kinematics, transmissions, sensors) is counted and reported; "
"``pc info`` shows the tally. :doc:`simulation` describes the gap and what"
" closing it would take."
msgstr ""
"连杆 *没有* 用来构建的那份几何体同样会被保留下来，作为零件 ``<assembly name>/<link "
"name>/<visual|collision>`` "
"：它已被定义、可以导出，但不会被放置到装配体中。完全无法表示的内容（关节运动学、传动装置、传感器）会被统计并报告出来； ``pc info`` "
"会显示这份统计。 :doc:`simulation` 说明了这一差距，以及弥合它需要什么。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:326
msgid ""
"The reverse direction is ``pc export -t urdf``, which writes a ``.urdf`` "
"file plus a directory of the STL files it references, from any part or "
"assembly. Each node of the assembly tree becomes a link, each "
"parent/child relation a fixed joint, and a shape used more than once is "
"written out once. What a part states about itself is written into the "
"URDF element that states it - the mass and inertia into ``<inertial>``, "
"the friction and contact properties into a ``<gazebo>`` block, the colour"
" into ``<material>`` - and only a part that says nothing gets inertial "
"properties computed from its geometry. A property PartCAD holds that URDF"
" has no way to state is reported rather than dropped in silence (see "
":doc:`simulation`)."
msgstr ""
"反方向是 ``pc export -t urdf`` ，它会从任意零件或装配体写出一个 ``.urdf`` 文件，以及一个存放它所引用的 STL "
"文件的目录。装配体树的每个节点都会变成一个连杆，每一对父/子关系都会变成一个固定关节，而被多次使用的形状只会被写出一次。零件关于自身的描述，会被写入表述它的那个"
" URDF 元素——质量和惯量写入 ``<inertial>`` ，摩擦与接触属性写入 ``<gazebo>`` 块，颜色写入 "
"``<material>`` ——并且只有什么都没说明的零件，才会根据其几何体计算出惯性属性。PartCAD 所持有而 URDF "
"无法表述的属性会被报告出来，而不是被悄悄丢弃（参见 :doc:`simulation` ）。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:337
msgid ""
"``pc convert assembly`` goes further than exporting: it rewrites the "
"package around the assembly and switches its declared type."
msgstr "``pc convert assembly`` 比导出走得更远：它会改写该装配体周围的包，并切换它所声明的类型。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:345
msgid ""
"Converting to ASSY writes an ``stl`` part for every link, an interface "
"pair for every joint, and an ``.assy`` that places its parts with "
"``connect:`` rather than with coordinates. Converting to URDF writes the "
"``.urdf`` and its meshes. Neither direction has an ad-hoc equivalent: "
"``pc adhoc convert`` refuses both formats, because an ASSY file is a set "
"of references to the parts of a package and a URDF becomes a part per "
"link - neither means anything without one."
msgstr ""
"转换为 ASSY 会为每个连杆写出一个 ``stl`` 零件、为每个关节写出一对接口，以及一个用 ``connect:`` "
"而不是坐标来放置其零件的 ``.assy`` 文件。转换为 URDF 则写出 ``.urdf`` 及其网格文件。这两个方向都没有对应的 adhoc"
" 形式： ``pc adhoc convert`` 对这两种格式都会拒绝，因为 ASSY 文件是一组对某个包中零件的引用，而 URDF "
"会变成每个连杆一个零件——离开了包，两者都毫无意义。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:353
msgid "Assembly YAML"
msgstr "Assembly YAML"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:355
msgid "Here is an example of an assembly defined using `Assembly YAML`:"
msgstr "下面是一个使用 `Assembly YAML` 定义的装配体示例："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:358 ../../source/config_product.rst:470
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "配置"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:358
msgid "Result"
msgstr "结果"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:386
msgid ""
"The example above shows an assembly created using ``Assembly YAML``. "
"Other methods to define assemblies are coming soon (e.g. using "
"``CadQuery`` or ``build123d``). The assembly file syntax is described in "
"the ``Assembly YAML`` section of this documentation."
msgstr ""
"上面的示例展示了一个使用 ``Assembly YAML`` 创建的装配体。定义装配体的其他方式即将推出（例如使用 ``CadQuery`` 或 "
"``build123d`` ）。装配体文件的语法在本文档的 ``Assembly YAML`` 一节中有描述。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:393
msgid "STEP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:395
msgid ""
"A STEP file that carries an assembly structure already says what an "
"assembly says: a tree of named components, each placed by a transform. "
"The ``step`` type reads it and uses it as the assembly itself, with no "
"intermediate file:"
msgstr ""
"带有装配结构的 STEP 文件，已经说出了装配体所要说的内容：一棵由具名组件构成的树，每个组件由一个变换来放置。 ``step`` "
"类型读取它，并直接把它当作装配体本身，不需要任何中间文件："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:407
msgid ""
"``pc add assembly step <file>.step`` writes that declaration for an "
"existing file."
msgstr "``pc add assembly step <file>.step`` 会为一个已有的文件写出这段声明。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:410
msgid ""
"Every component of the STEP file becomes an ordinary PartCAD part, named "
"``<assembly name>/<component name>``. Those parts are inspected, "
"rendered, exported and referenced from other assemblies like any other "
"part -- they are simply declared by the STEP file rather than by "
"``partcad.yaml``:"
msgstr ""
"STEP 文件中的每个组件都会变成一个普通的 PartCAD 零件，名为 ``<assembly name>/<component name>``"
" 。这些零件可以像其他任何零件一样被查看、渲染、导出，以及被其他装配体引用——它们只不过是由 STEP 文件而不是由 "
"``partcad.yaml`` 声明的："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:420
msgid ""
"A group inside the STEP file becomes a nested assembly, so the tree "
"PartCAD shows is the tree the CAD tool exported. Components that are the "
"same geometry in several places are recognized as one part placed several"
" times, which is what makes the bill of materials come out right."
msgstr ""
"STEP 文件内部的分组会变成嵌套的装配体，因此 PartCAD 显示的树就是 CAD "
"工具导出的那棵树。在多处出现、几何体相同的组件会被识别为同一个零件被放置了多次，正是这一点让物料清单的结果正确无误。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:425
msgid ""
"Nothing is written into the package: the geometry PartCAD extracts for "
"each component is derived data and lives in PartCAD's own internal state "
"directory. The source file itself does not have to be in the package "
"either -- with ``fileFrom``/``fileUrl`` (see :ref:`files`) a vendor's "
"STEP assembly is declared by its URL and downloaded the first time it is "
"used:"
msgstr ""
"不会有任何东西被写入包中：PartCAD 为每个组件提取的几何体属于派生数据，存放在 PartCAD "
"自己的内部状态目录里。源文件本身也不必位于包内——借助 ``fileFrom``/``fileUrl`` （参见 :ref:`files` "
"），供应商的 STEP 装配体可以用它的 URL 来声明，并在首次使用时下载："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:440
msgid "Compared to ``pc import assembly``"
msgstr "与 ``pc import assembly`` 的比较"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:442
msgid ""
"``pc import assembly`` reads the very same file with the very same "
"reader, but it is a one-shot conversion: it writes a STEP file per "
"component and an ``Assembly YAML`` file into the package, and from then "
"on the package owns them and the original file is never consulted again."
msgstr ""
"``pc import assembly`` 用完全相同的读取器读取完全相同的文件，但它是一次性的转换：它会向包中写入每个组件一个 STEP "
"文件，以及一个 ``Assembly YAML`` 文件；从此以后这些内容归包所有，原始文件再也不会被参考。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:447
msgid ""
"Use ``type: step`` when the STEP file is to remain the source of truth: a"
" vendor's file, a file regenerated by another CAD tool, or a file pulled "
"from a URL. Every change to it is picked up on the next use, and nothing "
"has to be kept in sync by hand."
msgstr ""
"当 STEP 文件要继续作为权威来源时，使用 ``type: step`` ：例如供应商的文件、由另一款 CAD 工具重新生成的文件，或从 URL"
" 拉取的文件。对它的每一次修改都会在下次使用时被采纳，不需要手工保持任何同步。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:452
msgid ""
"Use ``pc import assembly`` when the structure is to be taken over: the "
"resulting parts and ``.assy`` file are ordinary package content that can "
"be renamed, re-arranged, given interfaces and connections, or replaced "
"part by part."
msgstr ""
"当要把这个结构接管过来时，使用 ``pc import assembly`` ：由此产生的零件和 ``.assy`` "
"文件都是普通的包内容，可以重命名、重新编排、添加接口与连接，也可以逐个零件地替换。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:457
msgid "References"
msgstr "引用"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:459
msgid ""
"It is also possible to declare assemblies by referencing other assemblies"
" that are already defined elsewhere. Both methods work the same way they "
"do for :ref:`parts`: an assembly takes parameters like anything else, so "
"an assembly with other values is another instance of the same assembly, "
"and that is what an ``enrich`` of it asks for."
msgstr ""
"也可以通过引用别处已经定义好的其他装配体来声明装配体。这两种方式的工作原理与 :ref:`parts` "
"完全相同：装配体和其他东西一样接受参数，所以取用其他参数值的装配体是同一个装配体的另一个实例，而这正是对它做 ``enrich`` 时所要求的。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:469
msgid "Method"
msgstr "方式"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:471
msgid "Description"
msgstr "说明"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:472
msgid "Alias"
msgstr "Alias"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:479
msgid ""
"Create a shallow clone of the existing assembly. For example, to make it "
"easier to reference it locally."
msgstr ""
"创建现有装配体的一个浅层克隆。例如，为了更方便地在本地引用它。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:481
msgid "Enrich"
msgstr "Enrich"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:490
msgid ""
"Create an opinionated alternative to the existing assembly by setting "
"some of its parameters, the same way a part is enriched."
msgstr ""
"创建一个现有装配体的、带有既定倾向的替代版本，做法是设置它的部分参数，方式与零件被扩充的方式相同。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:494
msgid "Procurement"
msgstr "采购"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:496
msgid ""
"Not every assembly has to be assembled: some are sold assembled, as a kit"
" or as a pre-built module. Such an assembly is declared purchasable the "
"same way a part is (see :ref:`procurement`):"
msgstr ""
"并不是每个装配体都必须自己装配：有些是以组装好的形式出售的，可能是一套件，也可能是一个预制模块。这样的装配体声明为可购买的方式与零件相同（参见 "
":ref:`procurement` ）："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:509
msgid ""
"``vendor``, ``sku`` and ``count_per_sku`` have the same meaning as they "
"do for parts, with the assembly itself being what is ordered."
msgstr "``vendor`` 、 ``sku`` 和 ``count_per_sku`` 的含义与它们对零件的含义相同，只不过被订购的是装配体本身。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:520
msgid ""
"An assembly that has both ``vendor`` and ``sku`` set is considered "
"purchasable, and is not required to declare how it is manufactured: ``pc "
"test`` only checks that a supplier carries it. An assembly without them "
"is manufactured by producing its parts and putting them together, which "
"requires everything it is procured from -- its parts, and the sub-"
"assemblies that are sold assembled -- to be obtainable by itself."
msgstr ""
"同时设置了 ``vendor`` 和 ``sku`` 的装配体被视为可购买的，不需要声明它是如何制造的： ``pc test`` "
"只会检查是否有供应商供货。没有设置它们的装配体，则通过生产它的零件并把它们组装起来来制造，这就要求它所采购的一切——它的零件，以及那些以组装好的形式出售的子装配体——自身都能够获得。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:527
msgid ""
"Declaring an assembly purchasable does not stop it from being modelled "
"and rendered as usual: the links between its parts still describe what is"
" inside the box."
msgstr "把装配体声明为可购买的，并不妨碍它照常被建模和渲染：它各个零件之间的连接依然描述了盒子里面有什么。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:531
msgid ""
"This is also where ``pc supply find`` and ``pc supply quote`` stop "
"looking inside. An assembly is otherwise procured as the objects it is "
"made of, and the same question is asked about each sub-assembly in turn: "
"one that is sold assembled is ordered as a single item, and one that is "
"not is broken down further. Pass ``--recursive`` to order the parts even "
"where the assembly holding them could have been bought whole -- for "
"example to compare the cost of building it against the cost of buying it."
msgstr ""
"这也是 ``pc supply find`` 和 ``pc supply quote`` "
"停止向内查看的地方。在其他情况下，装配体会按照构成它的那些对象来采购，并对每一个子装配体依次提出同样的问题：以组装好的形式出售的，作为单个条目订购；不是这样的，则继续向下拆解。传入"
" ``--recursive`` ，即使持有这些零件的装配体本可以整体买下，也仍然订购这些零件——例如用来比较自行制造与直接购买的成本。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:548
msgid ""
"An assembly embedded in the parent's own source file (the nested "
"``links:`` of an Assembly YAML file) is not an object of any package, so "
"there is no name to order it by. Such an assembly is always procured as "
"its contents, and declaring a vendor for it has no effect."
msgstr ""
"嵌入在父级自身源文件中的装配体（Assembly YAML 文件里嵌套的 ``links:`` "
"）不是任何包的对象，因此没有可用来订购它的名称。这样的装配体始终按其内容来采购，为它声明供应商不会有任何效果。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:557
msgid "Scenes"
msgstr "场景"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:559
msgid ""
"A **scene** is a placed arrangement of objects: a workcell, a table with "
"the parts laid out on it, a simulation world. It is built the way an "
"assembly is, out of the very same files, and everything that works on an "
"assembly works on a scene -- it renders, it exports, it has a bill of "
"materials, ``pc ide view`` shows it."
msgstr ""
"**场景** "
"是对象的摆放布置：一个工作单元、一张摆着零件的工作台、一个仿真世界。它的构建方式与装配体相同，用的也是完全一样的文件；凡是对装配体有效的东西，对场景同样有效——它可以渲染、可以导出、有物料清单，"
" ``pc ide view`` 也能显示它。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:565
msgid ""
"What separates the two is intent, and one rule follows from it. An "
"assembly is a *product*: it says what it is made of and, through the "
"``how:`` section of each ``connect:``, how it is put together, which is "
"what the assembly instruction book (``pc render -t pdf``) is generated "
"from. A scene states only an end state. Nothing in it was assembled, so "
"there is nothing to say about the assembling, and ``how:`` is rejected "
"rather than ignored (see :doc:`assy`)."
msgstr ""
"区分两者的是意图，并由此引出一条规则。装配体是一件 *产品* ：它说明自己由什么构成，并通过每个 ``connect:`` 的 ``how:`` "
"小节说明它是如何装配起来的，而装配说明书（ ``pc render -t pdf`` "
"）正是由此生成的。场景只陈述一个最终状态。其中没有任何东西是被装配起来的，因此关于装配也就无话可说， ``how:`` 会被拒绝而不是被忽略（参见"
" :doc:`assy` ）。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:574
msgid "Declare scenes"
msgstr "声明场景"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:602
msgid ""
"The declaration points at the file that holds the scene and nothing else:"
" there is no assembly object in between. An ``.assy`` file in an "
"``assemblies:`` section is an assembly, and the very same file in a "
"``scenes:`` section is a scene."
msgstr ""
"声明只指向存放该场景的文件，别无其他：中间不存在任何装配体对象。位于 ``assemblies:`` 小节中的 ``.assy`` "
"文件是一个装配体，而完全相同的文件位于 ``scenes:`` 小节中则是一个场景。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:618
msgid "Scenes take parameters, aliases and enriches exactly as assemblies do:"
msgstr "场景接受参数、别名和 enrich 的方式与装配体完全相同："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:630
msgid "Gazebo worlds"
msgstr "Gazebo 世界"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:632
msgid ""
"The ``sim-gazebo:world`` type reads an `SDFormat <http://sdformat.org/>`_"
" ``.world`` file -- what Gazebo describes a simulation world in -- as a "
"scene directly, with no conversion step. It is declared by `partcad-sim-"
"gazebo <https://github.com/partcad/partcad-sim-gazebo>`_ rather than by "
"PartCAD itself, beside the exporter, the ``pc ide open`` entry and the "
"simulator that share their knowledge of the format, so a package that "
"uses it imports that package and names the type through it. Every model "
"is placed where its ``<pose>`` puts it, every link where its own pose "
"puts it inside the model, and every shape becomes a part of the package "
"named ``<scene>/<model>/<link>``. Those parts are ordinary parts: they "
"can be inspected, rendered and exported on their own."
msgstr ""
"``sim-gazebo:world`` 类型直接把 `SDFormat <http://sdformat.org/>`_ 的 "
"``.world`` 文件——Gazebo 用来描述仿真世界的格式——读取为场景，不需要任何转换步骤。它由 `partcad-sim-gazebo"
" <https://github.com/partcad/partcad-sim-gazebo>`_ 声明，而不是由 PartCAD "
"本身声明，与同样掌握该格式的导出器、 ``pc ide open`` "
"入口和仿真器放在一起；因此使用它的包需要导入那个包，并通过它来指名该类型。每个模型都放在它的 ``<pose>`` "
"所指定的位置，每个连杆放在它自身的位姿在模型内所指定的位置，而每个形状都会变成包中一个名为 ``<scene>/<model>/<link>`` "
"的零件。这些零件都是普通零件：它们可以被单独查看、渲染和导出。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:645
msgid ""
"\"SDF\" means two unrelated things in PartCAD. The ``sdf`` *part* type is"
" a signed distance function. This is **SDFormat**, and PartCAD calls it "
"``world`` throughout, after the files it lives in."
msgstr ""
"“SDF”在 PartCAD 中指两件互不相干的事情。 ``sdf`` *零件* 类型指的是有符号距离函数。而这里说的是 **SDFormat**"
" ，PartCAD 全程按它所在文件的名称把它称作 ``world`` 。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:649
msgid ""
"It is a best-effort reader: SDFormat describes a running simulation and a"
" scene describes where things are, so joints, lights, sensors, plugins, "
"actors, physics settings and the ground plane are counted and reported "
"rather than passed over in silence. ``pc info`` lists what was dropped. "
"See :doc:`simulation` for the whole picture."
msgstr ""
"这是一个尽力而为的读取器：SDFormat "
"描述的是一个正在运行的仿真，而场景描述的是东西在哪里，因此关节、灯光、传感器、插件、角色、物理设置和地平面都会被统计并报告出来，而不是被悄悄略过。"
" ``pc info`` 会列出被丢弃的内容。完整情况请参见 :doc:`simulation` 。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:655
msgid ""
"The reverse direction is the ``sim-gazebo:world`` export file type, "
"declared by the same package:"
msgstr "反方向是 ``sim-gazebo:world`` 导出文件类型，由同一个包声明："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:662
msgid ""
"and ``pc convert scene`` moves a scene between the two formats, rewriting"
" the package around it:"
msgstr "而 ``pc convert scene`` 可以在这两种格式之间转换场景，并改写它周围的包："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:670
msgid ""
"``pc import scene -t sim-gazebo:world warehouse.world`` does the first of"
" those in one step for a file the package does not declare yet, leaving "
"the package holding PartCAD's own objects. ``pc add scene sim-"
"gazebo:world warehouse.world`` declares the file where it lies instead."
msgstr ""
"对于包尚未声明的文件， ``pc import scene -t sim-gazebo:world warehouse.world`` "
"会一步完成上面的第一种转换，使包中留下 PartCAD 自己的对象。而 ``pc add scene sim-gazebo:world "
"warehouse.world`` 则是就地声明该文件。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:676
msgid "MuJoCo models"
msgstr "MuJoCo 模型"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:678
msgid ""
"The ``sim-mujoco:mjcf`` type reads a `MuJoCo <https://mujoco.org/>`_ "
"model as a scene, the same way ``sim-gazebo:world`` reads a Gazebo one. "
"It is declared by `partcad-sim-mujoco <https://github.com/partcad"
"/partcad-sim-mujoco>`_, for the reason the world type is declared by the "
"Gazebo one: every body is placed where its ``pos`` and orientation put it"
" inside the body that holds it, and every geom becomes a part of the "
"package named ``<scene>/<body>``."
msgstr ""
"``sim-mujoco:mjcf`` 类型把 `MuJoCo <https://mujoco.org/>`_ 模型读取为场景，方式与 "
"``sim-gazebo:world`` 读取 Gazebo 世界相同。它由 `partcad-sim-mujoco "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad-sim-mujoco>`_ 声明，原因与 world 类型由 Gazebo"
" 的那个包声明相同：每个 body 都放在它的 ``pos`` 和朝向在容纳它的 body 内所指定的位置，而每个 geom 都会变成包中一个名为"
" ``<scene>/<body>`` 的零件。"

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:685
msgid ""
"It is the one format that is **both** a scene type and an assembly type, "
"and which of the two a given file is depends on the section that declares"
" it rather than on the file. A URDF describes one robot and a ``.world`` "
"describes one world; an MJCF file is used for both -- the same element "
"holds a manipulator and the table it is bolted to -- and nothing in it "
"says which it is. So the package says so:"
msgstr ""
"它是唯一一种 **同时** 既是场景类型又是装配体类型的格式，而某个具体文件究竟属于哪一种，取决于声明它的小节，而不是文件本身。URDF "
"描述的是一个机器人， ``.world`` 描述的是一个世界；而 MJCF "
"文件两者都用——同一个元素里既有一台机械手，也有它被螺栓固定于其上的工作台——文件本身并不说明它是哪一种。于是由包来说明："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:704
msgid ""
"It is a best-effort reader in the same way the world reader is: joints, "
"actuators, tendons, sensors, lights, cameras, contacts and keyframes are "
"counted and reported, and ``pc info`` lists what was dropped. The reverse"
" direction is the ``sim-mujoco:mjcf`` export file type, which writes an "
"``.xml`` file plus the meshes it references:"
msgstr ""
"它和 world 读取器一样是尽力而为的读取器：关节、执行器、腱、传感器、灯光、相机、接触和关键帧都会被统计并报告出来，而 ``pc info``"
" 会列出被丢弃的内容。反方向是 ``sim-mujoco:mjcf`` 导出文件类型，它会写出一个 ``.xml`` 文件以及它所引用的网格文件："

#: ../../source/config_product.rst:715
msgid ""
"It is also the format ``pc sim`` hands a scene to MuJoCo in, and the one "
"``pc ide open --with mujoco`` expects a file to already be in; see "
":ref:`simulate`."
msgstr ""
"它也是 ``pc sim`` 把场景交给 MuJoCo 时所用的格式，以及 ``pc ide open --with mujoco`` "
"期望文件已经采用的格式；参见 :ref:`simulate` 。"

